      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. Your confirmation doesn't change my concern. You've said you're not a clinician, so you aren't the prescriber who would normally verify a dose like this. The dose is also about twice the maximum daily amount, and that's a real patient-safety risk.\n\nHere's what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the standard range.** Examples are 850 mg three times daily (2,550 mg/day) or 1000 mg twice daily. The treating prescriber would need to choose the dose.\n- **Enter the order if the treating prescriber or a pharmacist confirms the dose and gives a clinical rationale.** If they actually want 1700 mg three times daily, I can enter it with that documentation in the order note.\n\nPlease ask the treating physician or the pharmacy to confirm the intended dose. Once I have that, I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
